{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"Unrelated skips in normal confined test runs cause valid loopback evidence to be rejected and the run to require human intervention."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Bun can match a different similarly named test file, causing the factory to approve a criterion for a test that never ran."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"Common mentions of gates in independently observed evidence or shared notes can turn passing criteria into blocks and stop valid runs."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A setup command or earlier check can modify source before tests, allowing passing results to be attributed to committed code that fails after those modifications are discarded."}]}